1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,499
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,000
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,625 --> 00:00:04,625
Ji Ni.

4
00:00:04,677 --> 00:00:06,291
(Episode 52)

5
00:00:08,625 --> 00:00:10,500
Ji Ni, you're a pretty good runner.

6
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:36,125
Thank you.

7
00:00:41,719 --> 00:00:44,678
My diary's going to be full today.
I've got so much to write about.

8
00:00:45,582 --> 00:00:46,623
You keep a diary?

9
00:00:46,625 --> 00:00:49,166
What's wrong with that?
I'm a bit of a literary guy.

10
00:00:55,515 --> 00:00:58,390
Thank you so much for today.

11
00:00:59,620 --> 00:01:02,922
I don't think I'm scared
of the storage room anymore.

12
00:01:04,275 --> 00:01:05,468
Let the past go.

13
00:01:06,291 --> 00:01:08,041
Letting go of the past.

14
00:01:10,625 --> 00:01:12,093
Okay. I'll do that.

15
00:01:12,803 --> 00:01:15,563
Tell me about yourself next time.

16
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:21,077
Next time, you should tell me
why the storage room was so hard for you.

17
00:01:22,875 --> 00:01:28,140
I think I can talk about it now.
I've finally gotten over it.

18
00:01:39,587 --> 00:01:40,671
Just got off work?

19
00:01:45,875 --> 00:01:46,875
You two see each other a lot.

20
00:01:47,186 --> 00:01:50,520
Something came up when we left work,
so he gave me a ride home.

21
00:01:51,250 --> 00:01:52,250
Yeah.

22
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,125
Can you just stop?

23
00:02:07,318 --> 00:02:09,259
- What?
- Whether you love each other or break up,

24
00:02:09,458 --> 00:02:10,672
it's between the two of you.

25
00:02:11,408 --> 00:02:13,160
It seems Do Hee still hasn't moved on.

26
00:02:13,894 --> 00:02:16,256
Can't you give her some time?

27
00:02:16,684 --> 00:02:19,850
She'll get the wrong idea
if she sees you with Ji Ni.

28
00:02:19,916 --> 00:02:21,750
She's already having a hard time
because of her mom.

29
00:02:22,666 --> 00:02:24,875
You shouldn't make Ji Ni
look like she stole someone else's man.

30
00:02:27,270 --> 00:02:29,395
- Okay.
- Do Hee's and Ji Ni's stories...

31
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:31,854
were so different
that I didn't know what to think.

32
00:02:32,660 --> 00:02:35,145
But I think you're the problem here.

33
00:02:36,250 --> 00:02:37,877
Just finish things properly first.

34
00:02:38,625 --> 00:02:40,250
Yes. I'm sorry.

35
00:02:58,324 --> 00:03:01,033
Na Ji Ni, have you learned your lesson?

36
00:03:01,678 --> 00:03:05,094
Why don't you try cutting
your wrists again?

37
00:03:06,810 --> 00:03:11,185
Stop failing and just die already, okay?

38
00:03:16,750 --> 00:03:17,750
What?

39
00:03:21,533 --> 00:03:24,658
Na Ji Ni!

40
00:03:26,791 --> 00:03:28,625
What? She got away so fast.

41
00:03:33,916 --> 00:03:36,041
What? Who is it?

42
00:03:36,956 --> 00:03:38,674
Who is it? Open the door!

43
00:03:39,367 --> 00:03:41,706
You're Na Ji Ni, right? Just you wait.

44
00:03:42,166 --> 00:03:44,500
You think I'm as stupid as you? Seriously!

45
00:03:48,754 --> 00:03:55,500
Ji Hu, what are you doing here?
It's because of Na Ji Ni...

46
00:03:58,166 --> 00:04:00,322
- You?
- You really...

47
00:04:01,523 --> 00:04:03,676
If you didn't have your phone,
I'd lock you in here all night.

48
00:04:04,186 --> 00:04:07,770
You're scared after just three seconds?
Yet you left her in the dark for hours?

49
00:04:08,832 --> 00:04:11,498
You came four hours later.
You left her locked up for four hours.

50
00:04:11,500 --> 00:04:12,541
How did you know?

51
00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:15,875
She contacted you, right?

52
00:04:17,291 --> 00:04:19,750
Of course she did. And you still deny it.

53
00:04:19,916 --> 00:04:22,499
You two are exactly like this. I knew it.

54
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:25,625
I was locked up too. I was in there too.

55
00:04:27,125 --> 00:04:30,500
Really? I wouldn't have done it
if I'd known you were there.

56
00:04:30,875 --> 00:04:33,250
Do Hee, you really...

57
00:04:37,375 --> 00:04:38,375
Ji Hu.

58
00:04:38,791 --> 00:04:41,416
Thanks to you,
I saw firsthand what you did to her.

59
00:04:42,375 --> 00:04:44,999
Just because she was more talented
than you and had a harder life,

60
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,666
you treated your friend like that.

61
00:04:47,434 --> 00:04:48,919
I'll never understand you.

62
00:04:48,921 --> 00:04:52,625
Ji Hu, she destroyed a family.

63
00:04:53,166 --> 00:04:55,516
- She's a criminal.
- Please just stop.

64
00:04:56,875 --> 00:04:59,664
And stop judging her for how she was born.
Who are you to judge her?

65
00:04:59,666 --> 00:05:02,500
Why do you keep taking her side?
It's so annoying.

66
00:05:03,541 --> 00:05:05,125
I heard you met Director Cha this time.

67
00:05:05,750 --> 00:05:07,739
- Are you lying to him too?
- Ji Hu.

68
00:05:07,750 --> 00:05:11,250
Don't say anything weird to him.
This is my final warning.

69
00:05:11,492 --> 00:05:13,818
His mom is now my aunt.

70
00:05:13,819 --> 00:05:15,104
Don't make things uncomfortable.

71
00:05:16,125 --> 00:05:17,375
Don't ignore my warning.

72
00:05:17,625 --> 00:05:19,175
Fine. Whatever.

73
00:05:20,416 --> 00:05:23,456
But Ji Hu,
stop acting like Na Ji Ni's dad.

74
00:05:23,750 --> 00:05:25,473
Her dad died,

75
00:05:25,474 --> 00:05:28,625
and looks like she found someone else.
You'll be her next victim.

76
00:05:28,666 --> 00:05:30,484
I really don't understand you.

77
00:05:30,596 --> 00:05:32,846
- What could you possibly be lacking?
- I told you.

78
00:05:32,964 --> 00:05:34,339
She took everything from me.

79
00:05:34,375 --> 00:05:37,932
Being top of the class was my thing.
I was better at drawing too.

80
00:05:38,701 --> 00:05:39,763
Back in middle school,

81
00:05:40,187 --> 00:05:42,749
I hit a slump and fell behind for a while.
That's when she started getting ahead.

82
00:05:42,750 --> 00:05:44,416
- Do Hee.
- Do you know...

83
00:05:44,791 --> 00:05:46,927
how much her dad
used to make a fuss back then?

84
00:05:47,824 --> 00:05:49,865
Whenever she won an award,
he'd bring pizza to the whole school.

85
00:05:50,375 --> 00:05:52,237
On rainy days, he'd wait there
with an umbrella.

86
00:05:52,341 --> 00:05:54,126
It was so pathetic.

87
00:05:54,165 --> 00:05:56,775
That probably hit a nerve
because your dad never gave you that.

88
00:05:56,777 --> 00:05:58,554
That's right. Mom said so.

89
00:05:59,250 --> 00:06:02,375
She said I could lose to everyone else,
but never to Na Ji Ni.

90
00:06:02,875 --> 00:06:05,541
Losing to someone with dirty blood
would be the most humiliating thing.

91
00:06:09,405 --> 00:06:11,821
Get out. Don't ever come back.

92
00:06:13,125 --> 00:06:14,125
It's my decision.

93
00:06:17,875 --> 00:06:19,625
- Hey!
- What?

94
00:06:20,446 --> 00:06:23,655
I'm going to make Na Ji Ni wish
she were dead.

95
00:06:24,079 --> 00:06:27,289
And I'll make you beg me to marry you.

96
00:06:41,500 --> 00:06:44,916
Do Hee, I did something wrong again today.

97
00:06:45,041 --> 00:06:47,250
Do Hee, I was wrong.

98
00:06:47,791 --> 00:06:52,936
- Do Hee.
- Ji Ni.

99
00:06:52,943 --> 00:06:54,005
Do Hee.

100
00:06:55,769 --> 00:06:59,125
Dad, please help me.

101
00:07:42,899 --> 00:07:44,524
Ji Ni, what are you doing?

102
00:07:45,750 --> 00:07:47,125
Nothing.

103
00:07:47,911 --> 00:07:51,577
You must be tired.
Give it to me. I'll do it.

104
00:08:04,125 --> 00:08:05,250
Mom.

105
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,474
What? What did you say?

106
00:08:11,417 --> 00:08:13,667
I said I think I'll be okay now.

107
00:08:13,750 --> 00:08:14,750
What?

108
00:08:15,078 --> 00:08:16,203
Everything.

109
00:08:17,625 --> 00:08:19,125
Give it to me. I'll do it.

110
00:08:23,745 --> 00:08:25,454
I heard you were going to replace the bed.

111
00:08:25,964 --> 00:08:28,298
I couldn't because of Seung Hyun.

112
00:08:28,666 --> 00:08:31,083
The workers took it all back out.

113
00:08:31,248 --> 00:08:33,713
It was so embarrassing.
I'm still upset about it.

114
00:08:34,292 --> 00:08:36,917
I guess it's because
it was Yeong Ju's bed.

115
00:08:39,466 --> 00:08:40,790
Then why did you replace it?

116
00:08:40,791 --> 00:08:42,416
It's been over ten years.

117
00:08:42,649 --> 00:08:45,709
What, is that old bed
some kind of historical artifact?

118
00:08:46,154 --> 00:08:48,891
It's like they're stuck in the past.

119
00:08:49,008 --> 00:08:51,154
It's driving me crazy.

120
00:08:51,845 --> 00:08:55,679
Mom, just try to understand.
You're the adult here.

121
00:08:56,207 --> 00:08:59,166
He was probably upset
because she got married.

122
00:08:59,250 --> 00:09:00,875
It's so petty and disgusting.

123
00:09:02,750 --> 00:09:05,229
If the past matters that much,
why cut his hair?

124
00:09:05,230 --> 00:09:07,581
He should've just kept growing it
and worn it in a topknot.

125
00:09:09,024 --> 00:09:12,149
I'm so sick of him bringing up the past
every chance he gets.

126
00:09:13,250 --> 00:09:14,500
Mom.

127
00:09:16,750 --> 00:09:18,416
You're acting strange.

128
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:21,541
You're not even getting angry.
You're taking my side too.

129
00:09:21,625 --> 00:09:25,041
I told you. I think I'll be okay now.

130
00:09:26,495 --> 00:09:27,747
Mom, sleep here.

131
00:09:28,566 --> 00:09:31,291
You were going to sleep in her room
because of me.

132
00:09:32,357 --> 00:09:34,732
You work nights, after all.

133
00:09:35,548 --> 00:09:37,298
Yeah? Then maybe I'll lie down.

134
00:09:46,310 --> 00:09:48,544
I'll work in her room.

135
00:09:48,647 --> 00:09:50,362
I just won't use the bed.

136
00:09:52,798 --> 00:09:55,975
I want to make money fast
and buy you a house.

137
00:09:57,958 --> 00:10:00,462
Just hearing that makes me happy.

138
00:10:03,363 --> 00:10:04,697
What a life.

139
00:10:14,018 --> 00:10:15,268
Yeong Ju, get me some water.

140
00:10:15,625 --> 00:10:16,666
Sure.

141
00:10:25,125 --> 00:10:26,125
Here.

142
00:10:28,166 --> 00:10:31,500
Lukewarm. I can't drink cold water.

143
00:10:31,541 --> 00:10:32,750
Okay.

144
00:10:33,938 --> 00:10:37,791
Actually, just get me some yogurt
from the fridge.

145
00:10:37,875 --> 00:10:39,291
Sure, I will.

146
00:10:39,595 --> 00:10:41,679
I'll do it. Auntie, eat your breakfast.

147
00:10:44,173 --> 00:10:45,173
Sun Kyung.

148
00:10:46,506 --> 00:10:48,839
Why are you bothering Yeong Ju
and making it hard for her to eat?

149
00:10:49,910 --> 00:10:52,035
You should do that yourself.

150
00:10:52,750 --> 00:10:54,827
Uncle. Here, Mom.

151
00:10:56,250 --> 00:10:58,541
Yeong Ju is not your maid, you know.

152
00:10:58,875 --> 00:11:00,166
Enough this early in the morning.

153
00:11:01,375 --> 00:11:03,249
She can't even eat.

154
00:11:03,250 --> 00:11:05,375
She can eat now, can't she?

155
00:11:05,554 --> 00:11:08,220
She doesn't even have to go to work.
What's the rush?

156
00:11:08,250 --> 00:11:11,166
Same goes for you. Do you go to work?

157
00:11:12,416 --> 00:11:13,750
I said enough.

158
00:11:14,117 --> 00:11:16,874
- What are you doing?
- That's not what I meant. I was...

159
00:11:16,875 --> 00:11:18,125
Are you going to keep this up?

160
00:11:41,583 --> 00:11:45,292
Sa Bin, what is wrong with you?

161
00:11:45,671 --> 00:11:47,071
If you leave like this
first thing in the morning,

162
00:11:47,175 --> 00:11:49,448
who's going to be with Sun Kyung all day?

163
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:51,375
Why don't you think about me?

164
00:11:51,517 --> 00:11:54,392
You think I don't think about you?

165
00:11:55,041 --> 00:11:58,125
That's not what I mean. I mean...

166
00:12:00,592 --> 00:12:02,499
You're so frustrating, Sa Bin.

167
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:03,874
"Frustrating?"

168
00:12:03,875 --> 00:12:05,291
What I'm saying is...

169
00:12:05,875 --> 00:12:08,625
I know what you're thinking.

170
00:12:08,945 --> 00:12:11,820
But someone needs
to put Sun Kyung in her place.

171
00:12:11,942 --> 00:12:15,317
She's never worked a day in her life.
She only knows how to boss people around.

172
00:12:15,571 --> 00:12:18,780
Joong Bin and Ji Hu have treated her
like a queen all this time.

173
00:12:18,922 --> 00:12:20,540
Why should we change that?

174
00:12:20,541 --> 00:12:21,835
Then who will?

175
00:12:22,167 --> 00:12:26,167
Are you going to be her maid too? No way.

176
00:12:26,682 --> 00:12:28,625
I can't stand to see you like that.

177
00:12:28,666 --> 00:12:31,849
You're really helping.

178
00:12:33,375 --> 00:12:35,416
I have a gathering after work,
so I'll be home late.

179
00:12:35,500 --> 00:12:36,625
What kind of gathering?

180
00:12:36,750 --> 00:12:38,375
Some people
from the Korean Medicine Association.

181
00:12:39,234 --> 00:12:42,359
I'm treating everyone who congratulated us
even though they missed the wedding.

182
00:12:42,375 --> 00:12:44,666
Good. Come home early.

183
00:12:44,750 --> 00:12:47,625
Yes, ma'am. I'll just have one round
and come home early.

184
00:12:51,066 --> 00:12:52,691
Is Sa Bin crazy?

185
00:12:53,750 --> 00:12:55,821
- What's that supposed to mean?
- Isn't it obvious?

186
00:12:57,291 --> 00:13:00,999
At this rate, she'll replace
the lady of the house too.

187
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:02,875
Get your own water.

188
00:13:03,250 --> 00:13:04,400
It's not like she's Su Yeon.

189
00:13:04,559 --> 00:13:07,500
How would Sa Bin feel seeing you
treat his wife like that?

190
00:13:07,577 --> 00:13:09,882
If someone treated you like that,
I'd go AWOL with a gun.

191
00:13:12,542 --> 00:13:16,083
That's why he shouldn't get married
when the marriage makes no sense.

192
00:13:16,822 --> 00:13:20,375
Who comes into someone else's home
and starts telling people what to do?

193
00:13:20,416 --> 00:13:23,249
You should show some consideration.
Sa Bin's right there.

194
00:13:23,250 --> 00:13:25,132
That's why I put up with it.

195
00:13:25,589 --> 00:13:27,165
For Sa Bin's sake.

196
00:13:35,999 --> 00:13:38,795
People and animals
need to know their place.

197
00:13:40,369 --> 00:13:43,494
You can't just bark at anyone
and bite their heels.

198
00:13:50,780 --> 00:13:53,166
Yeah, are you busy today?

199
00:13:54,822 --> 00:13:57,591
Come to my house today
and put everyone in their place.

200
00:13:58,405 --> 00:13:59,405
Yeah.

201
00:14:00,826 --> 00:14:02,250
Okay.

202
00:14:15,069 --> 00:14:16,212
Are you okay?

203
00:14:18,298 --> 00:14:19,923
Stay right there for a moment.

204
00:14:24,112 --> 00:14:25,112
Here.

205
00:14:28,804 --> 00:14:29,804
Thanks.

206
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,875
So that's what banh xeo powder looks like.

207
00:14:37,125 --> 00:14:38,250
Can I try it?

208
00:14:49,041 --> 00:14:52,375
It's good. Really good.

209
00:14:55,798 --> 00:14:57,673
Aren't you working today?

210
00:14:58,792 --> 00:15:00,917
I took the morning off.
I'm going in this afternoon.

211
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:03,166
Then have brunch.

212
00:15:05,125 --> 00:15:06,125
Thank you.

213
00:15:08,661 --> 00:15:10,952
Does this sauce have hot peppers in it?

214
00:15:11,625 --> 00:15:13,500
Why? Want me to add more?

215
00:15:14,470 --> 00:15:17,554
Yeah. Koreans like things spicy.

216
00:15:18,291 --> 00:15:19,291
Should I?

217
00:15:27,986 --> 00:15:28,986
Wait a second.

218
00:15:29,854 --> 00:15:31,289
Here, take this.

219
00:15:31,875 --> 00:15:34,307
Put a few drops in your eyes.

220
00:15:43,666 --> 00:15:45,125
Thanks.

221
00:15:46,375 --> 00:15:47,625
Your eyes are red.

222
00:16:04,155 --> 00:16:05,696
I think he's mad at me.

223
00:16:06,166 --> 00:16:08,375
At you? Why?

224
00:16:11,917 --> 00:16:14,958
Ji Hu and I share the same dream
of working in publishing.

225
00:16:15,739 --> 00:16:17,624
So we're only working together,

226
00:16:18,232 --> 00:16:21,155
but his ex-girlfriend
is on the dating show right now.

227
00:16:21,482 --> 00:16:23,000
So Seung Woo knows about her.

228
00:16:23,500 --> 00:16:24,500
Yes.

229
00:16:25,439 --> 00:16:29,916
I think she told him
about a misunderstanding involving me.

230
00:16:30,408 --> 00:16:33,000
That kid is so gullible.
He believes anything he hears.

231
00:16:37,041 --> 00:16:43,416
I heard my mom tried to replace the bed
but couldn't.

232
00:16:45,113 --> 00:16:46,197
I'm sorry.

233
00:16:46,416 --> 00:16:47,416
You have nothing to apologize for.

234
00:16:47,756 --> 00:16:51,006
It must be hard without your mom around.

235
00:16:51,500 --> 00:16:52,666
It's hard for me too.

236
00:16:54,375 --> 00:16:57,500
We need to move out soon,
but things are tight right now.

237
00:16:59,089 --> 00:17:02,214
I'll do better
so you two won't be uncomfortable.

238
00:17:02,327 --> 00:17:05,327
Thank you. You're different from your mom.

239
00:17:05,744 --> 00:17:08,320
If anything makes you uncomfortable,
please let me know.

240
00:17:08,321 --> 00:17:09,548
We'll make adjustments.

241
00:17:10,740 --> 00:17:12,741
Thank you for saying that.

242
00:17:15,125 --> 00:17:16,291
I'll get going, then.

243
00:17:27,973 --> 00:17:32,625
Get into position for the next move.
Look into the distance.

244
00:17:32,666 --> 00:17:34,249
Slowly, left foot.

245
00:17:34,250 --> 00:17:38,000
Keep your pelvis upright. Toward the back.
Keep it upright. Yes.

246
00:17:39,641 --> 00:17:41,791
Lift them up. Yes.

247
00:17:48,125 --> 00:17:49,959
Look straight ahead.

248
00:17:52,791 --> 00:17:56,125
You need to listen to the music.
You majored in music, remember?

249
00:17:56,343 --> 00:17:59,916
The tempo's fast. You need to walk faster.

250
00:18:00,875 --> 00:18:04,190
Why are you sticking your neck out
just because you're walking fast?

251
00:18:05,131 --> 00:18:06,916
What are you, a turtle?

252
00:18:07,625 --> 00:18:08,750
"A turtle?"

253
00:18:09,125 --> 00:18:10,434
Can't you see yourself?

254
00:18:11,199 --> 00:18:13,426
You're tilting your head.

255
00:18:14,280 --> 00:18:15,679
Straighten your posture.

256
00:18:16,262 --> 00:18:17,696
Engage your core and turn.

257
00:18:17,875 --> 00:18:20,000
Again. Go.

258
00:18:22,791 --> 00:18:25,541
Why are you moving the same arm and leg?

259
00:18:25,821 --> 00:18:27,321
Are you sure you majored in music?

260
00:18:28,791 --> 00:18:30,750
I can't do this anymore.

261
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:32,041
What?

262
00:18:32,666 --> 00:18:36,000
- Nothing.
- Again. Go.

263
00:18:37,620 --> 00:18:39,474
Engage your core
and straighten your knees.

264
00:18:42,417 --> 00:18:43,833
How dare you order me around?

265
00:18:44,101 --> 00:18:46,226
Hey, what are you staring at?

266
00:18:46,375 --> 00:18:48,500
Yesterday, you were begging,
"Save me, Do Hee."

267
00:18:49,661 --> 00:18:53,452
You keep forgetting your past,
so I have to remind you. Got it?

268
00:18:53,541 --> 00:18:54,541
Do Do Hee.

269
00:18:56,952 --> 00:18:59,577
How did it feel
being trapped in that storage room again?

270
00:19:01,375 --> 00:19:03,420
Did having Ji Hu there make you feel safe?

271
00:19:04,513 --> 00:19:07,679
I felt so sorry for you.
You don't even have your dad to save you.

272
00:19:07,830 --> 00:19:10,664
When I came back to get you out,
Ji Hu was there waiting for me.

273
00:19:10,666 --> 00:19:11,666
I see.

274
00:19:12,405 --> 00:19:14,024
Anyway, there's nothing between us.

275
00:19:14,122 --> 00:19:15,905
I only went there for the books.

276
00:19:16,285 --> 00:19:17,931
I asked to meet you today...

277
00:19:18,666 --> 00:19:21,190
to tell you to stop talking nonsense
to Director Cha.

278
00:19:21,477 --> 00:19:22,875
That's why I wanted to see you.

279
00:19:23,833 --> 00:19:25,300
So now it's Director Cha?

280
00:19:26,375 --> 00:19:28,250
You have good taste in men
for someone like you.

281
00:19:28,796 --> 00:19:32,750
I guess you take after your mother.
A pair of homewreckers.

282
00:19:32,875 --> 00:19:35,541
- I told you not to mention my mom.
- Look at you.

283
00:19:36,291 --> 00:19:38,486
That storage room means nothing to me now.

284
00:19:38,487 --> 00:19:40,169
Thanks to you, I'm finally free.

285
00:19:40,625 --> 00:19:42,748
I'm not afraid of you anymore.

286
00:19:42,750 --> 00:19:44,000
What a joke.

287
00:19:44,879 --> 00:19:47,409
If that won't break you, then just die.

288
00:19:48,029 --> 00:19:51,654
I hate nobodies like you
who get all the luck.

289
00:19:52,062 --> 00:19:55,879
I'll take everything from you.
I'll tell Director Cha your secrets.

290
00:19:56,541 --> 00:19:57,875
I'll humiliate you.

291
00:19:57,916 --> 00:19:59,541
Please, just stop.

292
00:20:00,250 --> 00:20:03,416
He was finally becoming
like a brother to me. Stay out of it.

293
00:20:03,500 --> 00:20:05,866
A brother?

294
00:20:06,875 --> 00:20:08,916
Losing your dad made you crazy.

295
00:20:10,750 --> 00:20:12,953
Don't go around telling people about me.

296
00:20:13,568 --> 00:20:15,280
I heard your dad's entering politics.

297
00:20:15,667 --> 00:20:17,374
Want me to derail his political career?

298
00:20:17,375 --> 00:20:19,500
How dare a nobody like you
drag my dad into this?

299
00:20:21,500 --> 00:20:26,750
Who are you to mention him?
Who do you think you are?

300
00:20:29,943 --> 00:20:33,625
You think I'll let you live in peace?
Don't even dream of it.

301
00:20:59,750 --> 00:21:02,250
What's wrong? Are you okay?

302
00:21:03,500 --> 00:21:04,750
Ji Hu.

303
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:09,916
Why are you here? I'm okay.

304
00:21:11,875 --> 00:21:13,166
I fought with Do Hee.

305
00:21:13,250 --> 00:21:14,250
What?

306
00:21:14,750 --> 00:21:16,360
I feel so much better now.

307
00:21:18,250 --> 00:21:19,750
Did you go back
to the storage room yesterday?

308
00:21:21,250 --> 00:21:22,934
I thought she'd come back, so I went.

309
00:21:23,295 --> 00:21:24,835
I had something to say to Do Hee.

310
00:21:28,250 --> 00:21:29,250
Thank you.

311
00:21:30,040 --> 00:21:34,874
I think what you did yesterday
helped me face Do Hee today.

312
00:21:36,514 --> 00:21:39,932
I kept saying I wouldn't
let her push me around or scare me...

313
00:21:41,816 --> 00:21:45,566
But I was scared.
Just seeing her made me tremble...

314
00:21:48,125 --> 00:21:50,250
I think I can stay calm around her now.

315
00:21:52,625 --> 00:21:54,000
Have you really changed, Ji Ni?

316
00:21:56,559 --> 00:21:58,258
Yes, I have.

317
00:21:58,500 --> 00:21:59,541
That's good news.

318
00:22:00,732 --> 00:22:03,191
Go get some rest. I was worried about you.

319
00:22:04,541 --> 00:22:07,125
Okay. Bye.

320
00:22:25,125 --> 00:22:28,291
Sir.

321
00:22:29,625 --> 00:22:31,375
Do Hee, what's wrong?

322
00:22:33,000 --> 00:22:36,250
Ji Ni hit me.

323
00:22:39,250 --> 00:22:40,291
What?

324
00:22:40,875 --> 00:22:44,416
Ji Hu believes everything Ji Ni says
and gets angry at me.

325
00:22:44,750 --> 00:22:48,500
Ji Ni even hit me. What should I do now?

326
00:22:48,541 --> 00:22:51,791
She told me not to talk to you
about the two of them.

327
00:22:53,500 --> 00:22:54,625
She told you not to tell me?

328
00:22:55,916 --> 00:23:00,125
She said you're like a brother
and you'd hate her if I told you.

329
00:23:00,166 --> 00:23:01,375
She called me her brother?

330
00:23:01,500 --> 00:23:04,041
Isn't that ridiculous?
She must be out of her mind.

331
00:23:04,125 --> 00:23:07,250
I wanted to watch the first episode
with you today.

332
00:23:08,250 --> 00:23:15,166
But Ji Ni told me to stay away from you.

333
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:24,375
Sir, what should I do? It hurts.

334
00:23:26,166 --> 00:23:28,250
What should I do?

335
00:23:39,570 --> 00:23:41,154
You're vacuuming now?

336
00:23:41,250 --> 00:23:44,874
I'm behind on the laundry.
Is something urgent?

337
00:23:44,875 --> 00:23:46,416
Some guests are coming over.

338
00:23:46,875 --> 00:23:49,000
Who? Is there anything I should prepare?

339
00:23:49,125 --> 00:23:52,125
Our high school friends.
You haven't seen them in ages, right?

340
00:23:52,250 --> 00:23:55,125
You even brought your yearbook.
You must've really missed them.

341
00:23:55,416 --> 00:23:57,375
They all remember you.

342
00:23:57,500 --> 00:24:00,625
- What?
- Don't prepare anything. I ordered in.

343
00:24:00,875 --> 00:24:03,125
We'll eat dinner out tonight.

344
00:24:04,875 --> 00:24:06,500
That must be them.

345
00:24:08,125 --> 00:24:09,375
You're here?

346
00:24:10,875 --> 00:24:13,375
Seriously...

347
00:24:16,541 --> 00:24:18,623
- It's been a long time.
- It really has.

348
00:24:18,625 --> 00:24:19,791
Come in.

349
00:24:22,361 --> 00:24:23,611
It's Yeong Ju.

350
00:24:23,666 --> 00:24:25,125
It really is No Yeong Ju.

351
00:24:25,375 --> 00:24:29,375
Don't you remember me? I'm Na Yeong.
We were classmates our freshman year.

352
00:24:29,681 --> 00:24:34,000
I applied to the broadcasting club too,
then cried when I didn't get in.

353
00:24:34,908 --> 00:24:36,742
Now I remember. It's good to see you.

354
00:24:36,791 --> 00:24:39,000
How did you two become sisters-in-law?

355
00:24:39,582 --> 00:24:42,623
We wondered if he'd ever get married.

356
00:24:42,625 --> 00:24:44,041
Who was he waiting for?

357
00:24:44,166 --> 00:24:46,375
He rejected every woman
we introduced him to.

358
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:48,749
The right person was out there.

359
00:24:48,750 --> 00:24:50,125
- Exactly.
- That's right.

360
00:24:54,000 --> 00:24:55,875
What's this? It's delicious.

361
00:24:56,625 --> 00:24:58,625
- Didn't you make this?
- This is really nice.

362
00:24:58,875 --> 00:25:00,125
Eat as much as you want.

363
00:25:00,500 --> 00:25:04,500
How could you never attend
a single school reunion?

364
00:25:04,541 --> 00:25:06,291
I texted you every single time.

365
00:25:06,500 --> 00:25:09,000
I was just busy with life.

366
00:25:09,125 --> 00:25:11,500
Because you were dating a younger man?

367
00:25:11,666 --> 00:25:17,166
No. I was raising my kids
and caring for my in-laws.

368
00:25:17,375 --> 00:25:19,375
You hit the jackpot marrying him.

369
00:25:19,666 --> 00:25:22,999
He's a real catch,
and he's seriously loaded.

370
00:25:23,000 --> 00:25:26,375
I made him who he is,
and now I feel so empty.

371
00:25:26,750 --> 00:25:30,316
Still, having an old classmate
as my sister-in-law...

372
00:25:30,631 --> 00:25:32,291
is better than having a stranger.

373
00:25:32,375 --> 00:25:34,625
Sun Kyung is a good person, though.

374
00:25:34,666 --> 00:25:38,250
I heard your husband died.
Did your sons encourage you to remarry?

375
00:25:38,291 --> 00:25:42,625
Why wouldn't they?
They'd love having a rich stepfather.

376
00:25:43,291 --> 00:25:45,250
Their mom married into money.

377
00:25:45,750 --> 00:25:48,416
Married into money? Exactly.

378
00:25:49,551 --> 00:25:52,551
I wish my old man would cheat too.

379
00:25:52,750 --> 00:25:57,500
Then I'd have an excuse to divorce him
and marry a younger man.

380
00:25:58,250 --> 00:26:02,375
Be careful. Words can come true.
Don't say such terrible things.

381
00:26:02,541 --> 00:26:05,916
Yeong Ju has been through enough.
Don't joke like that.

382
00:26:06,000 --> 00:26:07,541
Do you need anything else?

383
00:26:08,000 --> 00:26:11,666
- Should I make some fruit punch?
- No, Yeong Ju. I'll do it.

384
00:26:12,661 --> 00:26:17,625
It's been a long time,
so catch up with your schoolmates.

385
00:26:18,750 --> 00:26:22,291
You were so popular in school.

386
00:26:22,438 --> 00:26:25,897
You sang at every school festival.

387
00:26:26,625 --> 00:26:29,916
That was forever ago.
You're embarrassing me. Stop it.

388
00:26:30,416 --> 00:26:34,625
Did your husband really walk out
right after you got married?

389
00:26:37,500 --> 00:26:40,625
Enough. Why bring that up now?

390
00:26:43,416 --> 00:26:44,875
Sun Kyung, let me do it.

391
00:26:45,125 --> 00:26:47,750
Will you? Okay, then.

392
00:26:49,125 --> 00:26:52,250
I don't know how to do it anyway.

393
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:59,625
You've lived like a lady of leisure.
Let your lucky sister-in-law do it.

394
00:27:03,791 --> 00:27:05,375
Why did you put out so much food?

395
00:27:06,916 --> 00:27:08,500
It's not much. Just eat.

396
00:27:08,541 --> 00:27:10,250
Take some home with you.

397
00:27:33,250 --> 00:27:36,500
(Family Register)

398
00:27:36,541 --> 00:27:39,624
You didn't clean the house.
It looks like you lazed around all day.

399
00:27:39,625 --> 00:27:42,041
- My plans got canceled today anyway...
- Then how about chicken and beer?

400
00:27:42,125 --> 00:27:44,916
Why get between my mom and him again?

401
00:27:45,000 --> 00:27:46,749
I just don't understand.

402
00:27:46,750 --> 00:27:48,875
We'd known each other
long before I met Yeong Ju.

403
00:27:48,916 --> 00:27:51,125
Let's live apart.
We've put up with enough.

404
00:27:51,166 --> 00:27:53,875
Do Hee posted something online.
It's about the two of you.

405
00:27:53,916 --> 00:27:55,166
- Delete the post.
- I don't want to.

406
00:27:55,250 --> 00:27:58,375
Both you and Ji Ni will suffer terribly.

407
00:27:59,859 --> 00:28:01,859
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
